From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:51:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] steamcompmgr: add scaling_filter and scaling_sharpness
 commands

Trying a filter on a device means writing the GAMESCOPE_NEW_SCALING_FILTER
atom with xprop against the right Xwayland display, and the sharpness
atom besides, which is slow enough that A/B comparisons get skipped.

Add a gamescopectl command that takes the same filter names as the
--filter option, sharing its name table so the two cannot drift, and a
sharpness command beside it, since the gamescopectl transport carries
one argument.
---
 src/main.cpp           | 17 +++----------
 src/main.hpp           | 23 +++++++++++++++++
 src/steamcompmgr.cpp   | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_upscale.cpp | 10 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

